-- title:
--   Failure of level raising at r: rank bound for `midML`
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to its maximal ideal, with finite residue field $k=$ `ResidueField 𝒪` and of characteristic zero, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a $2$-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p\in S$, and $N\neq 0$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$ and $r\nmid N$ such that for every valuation subring $P\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $r$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ (that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{r}$) one has $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ in $k$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$) to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, every $P$ lying over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Assume the two commutativity hypotheses: `BaseOpComm`, that the operators $\mathrm{baseOp}(g)=$ [`CohCarrier.heckeTL N ⊤ 𝒪 g.ℓ`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23) on $H^1(N,\top,\mathcal O)$ commute pairwise as $g$ ranges over the generator index set `Gen N r S` of admissible primes, and `MidOpComm`, the corresponding pairwise commutation of the operators $\mathrm{midOp}(g)$ on the auxiliary-level carrier. Then the $\mathcal O$-rank of `midML N r S 𝒪 θ hc₁`, the `ML` module of the Hecke data at level $Nr$ with operators $\mathrm{midOp}$ and residual eigensystem $g\mapsto\theta(T_{g.\ell})$, is at most twice the $\mathcal O$-rank of `baseML N r S 𝒪 θ hc₀`, the `ML` module of the corresponding Hecke data on $H^1(N,\top,\mathcal O)$.
--
--   This is the cohomological form of the failure of level raising at the auxiliary prime $r$ when $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\neq(r+1)^2$: the localised cohomology at level $Nr$ is no larger than two copies of the localised cohomology at level $N$, so that no eigenform new at $r$ contributes to the eigensystem $\theta$. It feeds the corresponding bound [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.finrank_ML_le_two_mul_finrank_baseML`](thm.html#CuspForm.AuxLevel.finrank_ML_le_two_mul_finrank_baseML) at the $\Gamma_0(N)\cap\Gamma_1(r)$ level used in the Taylor–Wiles patching argument.
-- source:
